// Pre-built road tiles: Japan's road network from OpenStreetMap, cut into square files, so the app can load a
// corridor's roads directly instead of building them from map tiles. Format and stitching rules: web/CONTRACT.md §7.
// scripts/build-tileset.mjs writes the tiles; readTileset() below turns the tiles under a route or a box back into
// the typed graph of CONTRACT §2 plus the hazards layer.
//
// A tile stores the network as OSM has it, not as the router sees it: links (an OSM way between two junctions, cut
// at every z13 tile border), each with its tag set, its bus / bicycle / ferry route set, its turn-restriction set and
// its tagged vertices; nodes with their tags and restriction sets; and only what needs the build's inputs: elevation
// (from the GSI DEM), the traffic estimate's measured inputs (road density, relief, betweenness) and the tunnel /
// footpath run lengths (worked out over the whole tileset). Tags are numbers into a dictionary, one per pack
// (CONTRACT §7b). The reader classifies the tags (osm-tags.mjs) every time it reads, decides which ways the graph has
// (keepWay: the tiles hold more, osm-tags.mjs storeWay) and works out the traffic estimate from its inputs, so a new
// rule, a new class or a refit of the traffic model is app code.
//
// A tile is three parts, each its own file in a pack's layer (CONTRACT §7b), so a change to elevations or to values
// worked out at build time re-ships that layer only: base (the network and its tags), elevation, derived (runs and
// the traffic inputs). Each part repeats the leaf and its node and link counts, so parts of two builds never mix.
//
// In memory a tile is a "link graph" L:
//   nodeX/nodeY   grid units (2^26 across the world, about 0.5 m in Japan); nodeShared 1 where the node is also in
//                 another tile (the same grid position there); nodeTs the node's tag set (0 = none); nodeZ in dm
//   linkA/linkB   end nodes; a link keeps its OSM way's direction (oneway, :forward / :backward depend on it)
//   coordStart    the link's points coordX/coordY, both ends included (they are the end nodes' positions)
//   linkTs/linkRs tag set and route set (0 = none); linkRr/nodeRr restriction set (0 = none); vtStart/vtIdx/vtTs the
//                 tagged vertices inside the link (point index, tag set); linkN the number of 20 m atoms (atomCount);
//                 zStart/linkZ the elevations (dm) at the n - 1 inner atom boundaries (none on bridges, tunnels and
//                 ferries: linear there); run the tunnel or footpath run in metres (0 = none); dens, relief, bc the
//                 traffic inputs, one byte each (encodeInputs; 0 = none)
//   dict          the dictionary its numbers refer to: { ways: [null, {k: v}], nodes: [null, {k: v}], rels: [{k: v}],
//                 rsets: [null, [relation index, ...]], rrsets: [null, [relation index * 4 + role, ...]] }, role 1 from,
//                 2 via, 3 to (a node's set: the restrictions it is the via node of)
import { corridor } from './route.mjs';
import { areaCorridor, driveSide } from './live/tiles.mjs';
import { SPEED, TRUCK, estimateV, encodeV } from './traffic.mjs';
import { COEFFS } from './traffic-coeffs.mjs';
import { chooseLod, chooseAreaLod, keepLink } from './live/lod.mjs';
